UID:9D06C667-6436-4014-9575-DCA344640F33
ATTENDEE;CUTYPE=INDIVIDUAL;ROLE=REQ-PARTICIPANT;PARTSTAT=ACCEPTED;CN=volteu
 ropa.org_3qtptk1l0mfg76gq9nfqq1h4mg@group.calendar.google.com;X-NUM-GUESTS=
 0:mailto:volteuropa.org_3qtptk1l0mfg76gq9nfqq1h4mg@group.calendar.google.co
 m
URL:https://luma.com/r27vwgfv
CREATED:20260816T125703Z
DESCRIPTION:​Are you a new citizen in Berlin and voting in a Berlin state e
 lection for the first time? Or simply curious about how politics and electi
 ons work here?\n\n​Join Black in Tech Berlin and Volt for an evening of con
 versation\, questions\, and practical insights ahead of the Berlin election
 .\n\n​We’ll explore:\n→ What does the Abgeordnetenhaus actually do?\n→ How 
 does voting in Berlin work?\n→ What should first-time voters know before he
 ading to the polls?\n→ What does it feel like to enter German politics as s
 omeone with an international background?\n→ And what questions do you have 
 about Berlin’s political future?\n\n​We’ll be joined by Pia Voltz\, founder
 \, district councillor in Treptow-Köpenick\, and candidate for the Berlin A
 bgeordnetenhaus with Volt\, for an open and honest conversation about navig
 ating German politics and participating in civic life.\n\n​Whether this is 
 your first time voting in Germany or you simply want to better understand h
 ow Berlin’s political system works\, come curious\, ask questions\, and mak
 e your voice count.
LAST-MODIFIED:20260816T125704Z
LOCATION:Volt Berlin\nChoriner Straße 34\, Prenzlauer Berg\, 10435 Berlin\,
  Deutschland
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:First Vote: Navigating Berlin's Election as New Citizens
TRANSP:OPAQUE
