UID:430252B4-2BF7-495C-A28E-CAF71D68AF69
CREATED:20190306T093844Z
DESCRIPTION:World temperatures are on a non-stop rising curve\, seas could 
 soon swallow Florida\, Mozambique or Amsterdam and meanwhile\, fish are cho
 king on plastic.\n\nIt’s paralyzing: what *on earth* can individuals do to 
 stop the madness? \n\nWhile awareness for climate change seems to be on the
  rise - even kids are protesting on the streets these days - individuals ca
 n face a numbing feeling of helplessness. “Climate anxiety” is a not-that-r
 ecent-anymore term coined by psychologists which describes a rising feeling
  of anxiety towards the (ecological) future currently spreading among the g
 lobal\, middle class population.\n\nBut: you’re not alone. And to prove tha
 t\, we invited a group of scientific experts\, activists and social entrepr
 eneurs - and equally anxious individuals - to help navigate those paralyzin
 g feelings and translate them into actions that bring change.\n\nJoin us to
  help answer these questions together:\n- What can and should be expected o
 f me as an individual to fight climate change?\n- What’s the role of corpor
 ations in this?\n- How can we speed up policies to support and implement re
 al structural change?\n\nJoin us!*\n\n*We’ll be welcoming you at Ecosia’s o
 ffices\, the search engine that plants trees (perhaps give it a try - plant
 ing trees for free helps reduce that anxiety for a few minutes a day ♥).\n\
 nConfirmed speakers:\nDr. Elisabeth Süßbauer\, Direction of the Cross Secti
 onal Research Area "Sustainability"\, Zentrum Technik und Gesellschaft\, TU
  Berlin\nMarie-Isabelle Heiss\, Volt Deutschland\nMore speakers TBC\n\nMode
 ration:\nAlexandra Schwarz-Schilling\, Entrepreneur and Climate Activist\n\
 nAgenda: \n18:30 - Doors Open \n19:00 - 19:15 Welcome from Ecosia and Volt\
 n19:15 - 20:00 Panel Discussion\n20:00 - 20:30 Networking\n\n\nPlease regis
 ter for the event here: https://www.facebook.com/events/495696440961305/
LAST-MODIFIED:20190410T111739Z
LOCATION:haus ungarn\, Karl-Liebknecht-Str. 9\, 10178 Berlin\, Germany
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Panel Discussion: How do we unf**k the planet?
TRANSP:OPAQUE
X-APPLE-TRAVEL-ADVISORY-BEHAVIOR:AUTOMATIC
END:VEVENT
