DESCRIPTION:THIS EVENT WILL BE HELD IN ENGLISH.<br><br>In the European Parl
 iament\, only 41% of our MEPs identify as women. While this is up from 16% 
 in 1969\, there is still room to improve.<br><br>Join this all-female panel
  to learn first-hand about the difficulties women face in politics and how 
 Volt is approaching this challenge.<br><br>Panelists:<br><ul><li>Julia Boeh
 me\, (Social Equality Co-Facilitator Volt Europa &amp\; Co-Petitioner of th
 e&nbsp\;<a href="https://www.instagram.com/explore/tags/stophomelessness/">
 #stophomelessness</a>&nbsp\;petition) will be joined by:</li><li>Alexandra 
 Barsuhn\, Volt Co-President of Rhineland - Palatinate</li><li>Anouk Ooms\, 
 General Secretary of Volt Europa &amp\; Diversity and Inclusiveness Trainer
 </li><li>Daniela Ramos Giraldo\, Communications Strategist</li><li>Mihaela 
 Siritanu\, Treasurer Volt Europa&nbsp\;&nbsp\;</li></ul>
LAST-MODIFIED:20201027T235341Z
LOCATION:Link will be added soon!
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Why aren't women equally represented in politics? (English!)
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
