UID:702C0AA5-BE8F-4413-8548-F451D43F3DB1
RECURRENCE-ID;TZID=Europe/Berlin:20260317T180000
CREATED:20251118T220821Z
DESCRIPTION:Resilienz nicht nur sagen\, sondern machen. Ein Abend bei Volti
  Nico Gramenz im takeKONTROL Resilience Solutions Lab in Alt-Hohenschönhaus
 en (takeKONTROL Resilience Solutions Lab\, Weißenseer Weg 37\, 13055 Berlin
 \,  H-Tor\, 7.OG)\n\nJeden 3. Dienstag im Monat veranstalten wir einen Südo
 st-Themenabend\, in dem wir aktuelle Themen der Bezirke in Südost bespreche
 n\, die für die BVV und das AGH relevant sind. Hierbei schauen wir uns vor 
 Ort die Gegebenheiten an und diskutieren die Themen dann in einem nahe gele
 genen Lokal. Dementsprechend wechseln wir je nach Thema die Bezirke und Ort
 e\, an denen wir uns treffen.\nAlle Südost-Mitglieder\, insbesondere die Ka
 ndidierenden für die BVV und das AGH sind herzlich willkommen 💜
LAST-MODIFIED:20260519T085435Z
LOCATION:Weißenseer Weg 37\, 13055 Berlin ( H-Tor\, 7.OG)
SEQUENCE:1
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:[Südost] Bezirks-Themenabend: Kritische Infrastruktur in Berlin: We
 r bist du\, wenn der Krieg kommt? Wie wir Frieden bewahren und was jede/r v
 on uns dabei tun kann. 
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20190416T163000Z
DTEND:20190416T183000Z
DTSTAMP:20260816T152803Z
UID:2D178274-F07A-4633-9AAA-E6E97288EF5B
CREATED:20190228T085756Z
DESCRIPTION:From driverless vehicles to machine learning and industrial aut
 omation\, much of the discussion on artificial intelligence tends to focus 
 on how technology will disrupt society in the coming years. According to so
 me projections\, automation could threaten as many as 800 million jobs worl
 dwide by 2030\, while leading to other consequences like growing income ine
 quality and fewer opportunities for social mobility.\n\nBut what are the op
 portunities for human and social progress in a future driven by AI?  How ca
 n we ensure that new technology is implemented in a way that respects and s
 trengthens individual freedom\, democratic values\, and social well-being\,
  rather than threatening them?  When it comes to these questions\, Europe i
 s in a unique position to shape the conversation\, but only if it commits t
 o being a leader rather than a bystander in the development of AI.\n\nWhat 
 are the ongoing implications of artificial intelligence in society?  And wh
 at changes are we dealing with already? Join an interactive panel of policy
  experts\, activists\, and entrepreneurs for a vibrant discussion of what t
 he future of AI might hold\, and what role Europe should play.\n\nConfirmed
  speakers:\n\nDamian Boeselager\, Co-Founder\, Volt Europa\nProf. Dagmar Mo
 nett-Diaz from the Berlin School of Economics.\n\nMore speakers TBC\n\n\nAg
 enda: \n\n\n6:30pm - Doors Open\n7:00pm - 7:15pm Welcome from Factory Berli
 n and Volt\n7:15pm - 8:00pm Panel Discussion\n8:00pm - 8:30pm Networking\n\
 n\nPlease register for the event here: https://www.facebook.com/events/5149
 97172359217/
LAST-MODIFIED:20190413T152408Z
LOCATION:Factory Berlin\nRheinsberger Straße 76/7710115 Berlin 10115 Berlin
  DE
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Panel Discussion: What is Europe's role in shaping an AI future?
TRANSP:OPAQUE
