UID:4harufkp80d7i8nlhf6stf6sfu@google.com
CREATED:20210331T103645Z
DESCRIPTION:<b><p>Did you know that you\, as an EU citizen registered in Be
 rlin\, are eligible to vote in the Berlin District Council (the <i>Bezirksv
 erordnetenversammlung</i>\, or <i>BVV</i> in short) this September?</p><p><
 b>The District Council is a very important political body that decides abou
 t all the things going on right in front of your doorstep: This could be ev
 erything from the location of new bike lanes or green spaces to which NGOs 
 will be supported in your area.&nbsp\;</b></p></b>This is your city\, too -
  and you should make your voice heard.<br><br>So how can you vote?<br><br>W
 e'll help you make sense of the bureaucracy and explain which steps to take
  to vote. It's really rather simple\, we promise.<br><br>Just pop by for a 
 beer\, a chat\, and some info.<br><br>No prior knowledge of Germany's polit
 ical or party system is necessary - just come as you are.<br>&nbsp\;<br>Joi
 n us at <b>7 pm</b>&nbsp\;at Späti Campus in Weserstraße/Weichselstraße.<br
 ><br>See you there!<br><br>P.S. If you can't make it today\, join any of th
 e following events:<br><br>28. July in Neukölln<br>25. August in Mitte<br>2
 2. September in Friedrichshain-Kreuzberg
LAST-MODIFIED:20220603T053000Z
LOCATION:Späti Campus\, Weichselstraße 54\, 12045 Berlin\, Germany
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:EU Can Vote! // Info Event for EU residents
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
DTSTART:20240927T180000Z
DTEND:20240927T210000Z
DTSTAMP:20260816T152803Z
UID:tsd14ebjpn5ko05hvkukjtqlho@google.com
CREATED:20240914T121337Z
DESCRIPTION:Get your free Ticket: https://www.eventbrite.com/e/standing-tog
 ether-engaging-in-dialogue-on-the-israelpalestine-conflict-tickets-10172994
 69097?utm_experiment=test_share_listing&aff=ebdsshios \n\nWe are excited to
  invite you to a crucial event that marks a significant step in the develop
 ment of our stances on the Israel/Palestine conflict. Founders of Standing 
  Together https://www.standing-together.org/en\, Alon-Lee Green and Rula Da
 ood\, are travelling to Amsterdam in September and we have been given the u
 nique opportunity to meet them. Standing Together is a progressive grassroo
 ts movement mobilizing Jewish and Palestinian citizens of Israel against th
 e occupation and for peace\, equality\, and social justice. As a Jewish Isr
 aeli and a Palestinian citizen of Israel\, Alon-Lee Green and Rula Daood ar
 e committed to show us how both groups can work together to create a better
  reality for Israelis and Palestinians.\n\nAs a political organisation comm
 itted to speaking with one voice on behalf of its members\, we recognise th
 e challenges and importance of finding common ground on the Israel/Palestin
 e conflict. That is why we are excited to be able to give our community the
  opportunity to talk to and learn from Standing Together. This event will e
 xpose us to perspectives that are often underrepresented in the media and i
 n our internal discussions. It will help guide us to engage in open\, inclu
 sive\, and informed discussions on the conflict.\n\nConfirmed speakers (mor
 e speakers to follow):\n\n•Alon-Lee Green & Rula Daood (Founders of Standin
 g Together)\n\n•Anna Strolenberg (MEP)\n\n•Francesca Romana D'Antuono (co-p
 resident)\n\n•Marieke Koekkoek (Dutch MP)\n\n•Amsterdam City Councillors It
 ay Garmy (Volt) & Sheher Khan (DENK)\n\nThe goal of this event is to create
  a safe environment for our members and political representatives to come t
 ogether\, engage with experts\, and gain a deeper understanding of the on-t
 he-ground realities in Israel and Palestine. An understanding that can help
  our leaders stand for change in politics\, and equip our community with mo
 re empathy towards each other as well as the people living these horrors in
  Israel and Palestine.\n\nSheher Khan and Itay Garmy will also join the con
 versation. Despite their differences\, Sheher and Itay\, both Amsterdam Cit
 y Councillors\, have worked closely together to bridge divides. Itay is a J
 ewish and Israeli representative for Volt\, while Sheher\, representing DEN
 K\, is a Muslim and pro-Palestinian activist. Together\, they initiated the
  "Known Makes Loved" (in Dutch: Bekend maakt Bemind) project\, which was un
 animously adopted by the Amsterdam City Council just five days after Octobe
 r 7th. Their initiative seeks to build connections among groups of citizens
  who might otherwise never interact or may hold prejudices against one anot
 her.\n\nThis event is meant to be the first of a cycle of events and initia
 tives designed to support and consolidate our political positioning on the 
 Israel/Palestine conflict. While this starts as a Volt Europa project (host
 ed in collaboration with Volt Netherlands)\, we believe the way forward as 
 a community is the participation and involvement of national and local team
 s in a true pan-European fashion.\n\nWe will come together to watch the eve
 nt streaming\, and discuss it collectively\, to create awareness and unders
 tanding.\n\nWe look forward to your participation in this important dialogu
 e\, as we continue our journey to understand and support effective solution
 s for the Israel/Palestine conflict.\n\nTogether\, let’s make a difference.
LAST-MODIFIED:20240914T125011Z
LOCATION:Choriner Str. 34\, 10435 Berlin\, Deutschland
SEQUENCE:0
STATUS:CONFIRMED
SUMMARY:Standing Together - Engaging in Dialogue on the Israel/Palestine Co
 nflict - Watchparty & Discussion
TRANSP:OPAQUE
END:VEVENT
